Text:
fearlessMessage is a program that sends one Message to the 'single' manager, and prints the Answer of the 'single' manager on its standard output.
A Message about a folder holds a Target: the 'name' of that folder as a ProjectName, optionally followed by the path of that folder as a Base16.
The 'name' of a folder is ProjectName when ProjectName.fearless is the only file at top level in that folder whose name ends with ".fearless".

Grammar:
Message ::= "EditMetadata " Base16                                     \
          | "Register " Base16                                         \
          | "Forget " Target                                           \
          | "Kind " Target " " Kind                                    \
          | "Mount " Target " " TypeName " " Target'                   \
          | "Unmount " Target " " TypeName                             \
          | "Attenuate " Target " " TypeName " " TypeName1 " ".." " TypeNamen  \
          | "SelectMains " Target " " TypeName1 " ".." " TypeNamen
Target ::= ProjectName | ProjectName " " Base16
Base16 ::= "Base16:" ([0-9A-F][0-9A-F])+
Answer ::= "Applied\n" | "Refused\n" Error
Error ::= ...

Well formedness:
in Message: all TypeName of a SelectMains are disjoint
in Base16: second component is a valid OS FS path when decoded

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with syntax   fearlessMessage "Message"
B action fearlessMessage sends Message to the 'single' manager and opens a port to read...//this should be much longer
C after fearlessMessage prints the Answer of the 'single' manager//No! else it would only be printing when the port is closed?
